## Missing / weaker areas (not blocking a PASS, but worth tightening)

1. **Static HTML path vs live DOM** — `ksVisualHashReportFromHtmlBlob` only collects valid 3-letter markers; it does **not** populate `invalidRaw`, `mismatches`, or `incompleteMarkers` ```46:72:tools/website-ux-auditor/lib/visual-catalog.js
export function ksVisualHashReportFromHtmlBlob(blob) {
  // ...
  return {
    validUnique: [...seen].sort(),
    invalidRaw: [],
    mismatches: [],
    incompleteMarkers: [],
    instanceCountByHash,
  };
}
```  
   So static-only runs under-report hash governance relative to Playwright (invalid / pair / mismatch findings need the live DOM report).

2. **Test breadth** — Fixtures cover registry load, unknown hash (with `selector` / severity), registry missing, DOM mismatch + duplicate instances without catalog, registry duplicate once-per-ctx, HTML blob discovery, and coverage rollup. There are **no** dedicated tests for every finding id (e.g. deprecated, incomplete marker, invalid raw, missing contract ref, missing contract file).

3. **Independent re-check of `npm test`** — In Ask mode this session did not execute `npm test`; acceptance is taken from the phase doc plus code review. Re-run locally if you need machine-verified proof today.

